=== ARTICLE: Complexion - under the hood ===
[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/groups.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]How a look is chosen[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Who someone is decides.[/b] Every kind of overlay can go to anyone, but how likely each kind is depends on who they are. Raiders get many tattoos, scars and marks; settlers look ordinary. 22 groups by faction and place each have their own odds and styles: the gangs and factions, and places such as Diamond City, Covenant, Goodneighbor, caravans, farmers and scavengers.[/*]
[*][b]An everyday layer for everyone.[/b] Moles, skin detail, body and pubic hair go to people of every faction, and often.[/*]
[*][b]Rough living.[/b] Grime, blood, open wounds, pustules and fresh bruises go only to people who live rough: nobody in Diamond City, Covenant, the Brotherhood, the Institute or Vault 81; a few settlers, farmers and caravan hands; about a fifth of Goodneighbor; around half of raiders, Disciples, captives and scavengers.[/*]
[*][b]Age and skin tone.[/b] Grey hair means old: no acne, but age spots and veins. Freckles, sunburn and redness go on pale and light skin only, tan lines up to olive skin.[/*]
[*][b]How many.[/b] The count is drawn per group (settlers usually 1 to 3, raiders 3 to 6) under one hard cap of 6 per person. Each overlay is a full copy of the skin, so the cap keeps the game light.[/*]
[*][b]A whole look, not a pile.[/b] The composition is weighted as a whole: three different kinds rather than three of the same, one style per person, no two tattoos on one spot, and a faction's emblem only on its own people.[/*]
[*][b]Men too.[/b] Men get the same everyday layer women do (moles, scars, grime, pubic hair), painted by Complexion because the packs give men only body hair and tattoos.[/*]
[*][b]Adult pieces[/b] (slave stamps, chains, sexual tattoos) go to raiders' captives, and to raiders and the Nuka-World gangs at low odds. One MCM switch turns all of them off.[/*]
[*][b]Named characters.[/b] 59 characters have a look of their own from their stories, matched before any faction: Cait scarred and bruised from the Combat Zone, Piper all but plain, Danse scarred under the Brotherhood's mark, Fahrenheit inked. Ivy is left alone: her look belongs to her own mod.[/*]
[*][b]Decided once.[/b] Each person's look is decided the first time you meet them and kept. A look picked by hand in the window stays their look until you roll it again. After an update with new rules, a look that no longer fits is chosen again once, the next time you meet that person.[/*]
[/list]
[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/composition.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]Living beside other mods[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Other mods' overlays are kept.[/b] Complexion remembers which overlays it added. When it changes someone, it rebuilds their list and puts every other mod's overlay back. Its own sit underneath, so AAF's and Rapport's (sweat, for example) always draw on top.[/*]
[*][b]AAF scenes are left alone.[/b] Nobody is changed during an AAF scene, because AAF keeps hold of the overlays it put on people. Between scenes it is safe: AAF asks again for its next set.[/*]
[*][b]Every overlay is checked.[/b] After adding, Complexion checks that each of its overlays is really there, and if one went missing it rebuilds that person cleanly once.[/*]
[*][b]Random Overlay Framework can stay.[/b] Invictusblade's tattoo packs need ROF's plugin, so uninstalling ROF would lose them. With RobCo Patcher installed, Complexion switches ROF's handing-out off: it marks every human and ghoul as "already done" in ROF's own terms, without touching ROF's files or anything your save depends on. It checks this when the game starts and tells you either way.[/*]
[/list]
[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/cheap.jpg[/img][/center]
[center]One decision per person and one rebuild, ever: no cloak spell, no waits, no faction scans in scripts.[/center]

[size=4][b]How the marks are painted[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Painted on the body in 3D.[/b] Complexion's 706 overlays are painted on the CBBE and male bodies in 3D and baked into the body's own texture layout, so a bruise is a whole blob around a point on the body, even across texture seams.[/*]
[*][b]They multiply the skin.[/b] Each mark darkens (grime, bruises, blood, moles, hair) or lightens (old scars) the skin under it, lit and shadowed with it, on any skin tone. An early version blended them instead, and pale scars glowed like neon in dark corners; multiplying fixed that.[/*]
[*][b]No hard edges at the neck and wrists.[/b] The body mesh ends at the neck and the wrists, where the head and hands begin. Every mark fades out over the last few centimetres before those seams, so a sunburn never ends in a line against a pale head. Marks that belong there (a collar's chafe, rope marks) keep their edge.[/*]
[*][b]A realism layer of its own:[/b] moles, freckles, birthmarks, pores, veins, stretch marks, areola detail, pubic and body hair in styles and colours.[/*]
[*][b]Traditional flash tattoos:[/b] roses, skulls, daggers, swallows, anchors, snakes, the nautical star, the mushroom cloud, a Nuka-Cola cap and more, in bold American-traditional style, the kind a wasteland tattooist would ink. With these, the LoversLab packs are optional.[/*]
[*][b]Measured places.[/b] Where a mark sits (chest, nape, navel, hips, thighs) is measured on each body from landmarks such as the nipples and the crotch, never assumed at a fixed height.[/*]
[/list]
[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@68961e61bd0355ff3bf7a5f61a0e68916a5d8424/docs/img/marks.jpg[/img][/center]

[size=4][b]The overlay window[/b][/size]
The window is built like Silhouette's picker. Aim at someone ("Them") or at no one ("Me", your own character) and press its hotkey. The person stands still and undressed, the camera frames them, and the window lists every overlay that fits them, Complexion's own and your packs', by category with a search and pictures. Several overlays per category can be switched on and off; each change shows live. Putting one on moves the camera close to where it sits, and [i]Whole body[/i] goes back. Apply keeps the look; Cancel puts back exactly what they had, clothes included. You are never given a random look: the window is how you give yourself overlays.
[center][img]https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/ReidenXerx/fo4-complexion@d79ece3a24ba1c96fb9883533656cf450c150245/docs/img/window.jpg[/img][/center]
